From fb78a3b7ab759f61df4f7d6fa394a6e5ebff3a2a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
Date: Mon, 24 Aug 2026 15:38:02 +0200
Subject: [PATCH ath-next v5 1/9] wifi: ath11k: free tx skbs through
 ieee80211_free_txskb()

ath11k_dp_tx_free_txbuf(), reached from the HTT tx completion handler
for the REINJ and INSPECT statuses, frees the frame with
dev_kfree_skb_any(). Every other tx completion path in dp_tx.c hands the
skb back to mac80211.

dev_kfree_skb_any() leaks the tx status clone and idr entry mac80211
keeps for a frame whose socket asked for status. Commit 29d15589f084
("wifi: ath11k: Cleanup mac80211 references on failure during tx_complete")
fixed the same leak on three sibling paths. With
NL80211_EXT_FEATURE_AQL, which the next patch sets, it also keeps the
airtime the frame was charged at dequeue, and once the access category
reaches its limit no station on the radio is scheduled in it again.

Free the frame with ieee80211_free_txskb(). Neither status was seen on
the hardware below, so the change is by inspection.

Tested-on: IPQ8074 hw2.0 AHB WLAN.HK.2.9.0.1-02146-QCAHKSWPL_SILICONZ-1

Fixes: d5c65159f289 ("ath11k: driver for Qualcomm IEEE 802.11ax devices")
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Signed-off-by: Julius Bairaktaris <julius@bairaktaris.de>
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/dp_tx.c
@@ -305,9 +305,10 @@ static void ath11k_dp_tx_free_txbuf(stru
 	skb_cb = ATH11K_SKB_CB(msdu);
 
 	dma_unmap_single(ab->dev, skb_cb->paddr, msdu->len, DMA_TO_DEVICE);
-	dev_kfree_skb_any(msdu);
 
 	ar = ab->pdevs[mac_id].ar;
+	ieee80211_free_txskb(ar->hw, msdu);
+
 	if (atomic_dec_and_test(&ar->dp.num_tx_pending))
 		wake_up(&ar->dp.tx_empty_waitq);
 }
